      [35m	›› {
      	     "comment": "I think each plugin should output JSON not html as it is not reliable to parse nor manipulate and requires `window` instance to be instantiated which is annoying on `node` based projects. \r\n\r\nHaving a plugin handling commenting seems quite weird as commenting is done by calling Octokit and the REST api which is already a library by itself, so no need to encapsulate it within another one to do the same thing.\r\n\r\nMy view on this, is to finalize [https://github.com/ubiquity-os/permit-generation/issues/5](https://github.com/ubiquity-os/permit-generation/issues/5) to import it withing the `conversation-reward` that will post the comment itself as well, otherwise the architecture will be quite convoluted doing ping pong with everything.",
      	     "html": "<p>I think each plugin should output JSON not html as it is not reliable to parse nor manipulate and requires <code>window</code> instance to be instantiated which is annoying on <code>node</code> based projects. </p>\n<p>Having a plugin handling commenting seems quite weird as commenting is done by calling Octokit and the REST api which is already a library by itself, so no need to encapsulate it within another one to do the same thing.</p>\n<p>My view on this, is to finalize <a href=\"https://github.com/ubiquity-os/permit-generation/issues/5\">https://github.com/ubiquity-os/permit-generation/issues/5</a> to import it withing the <code>conversation-reward</code> that will post the comment itself as well, otherwise the architecture will be quite convoluted doing ping pong with everything.</p>\n",
      	     "caller": "FormattingEvaluatorModule.debug"
      	   }[0m

